+# growth.dem — Story 5.1: deterministic map growth + spawn validity (E31).
+# The fixture (residential(0) ← router(1) → content_host(2)) is the seed; the
+# director's map-growth branch (ODN-7, growth.odin) spawns TERMINALS outward
+# from the player-placed router mesh — one per 6 s window
+# (GROWTH_INTERVAL_TICKS = 120 @ 20 Hz), deterministically from the seed + the
+# executed tick (NEVER wall-clock): same seed -> identical growth timeline
+# (replay byte-identical — the growth is seed-derived, so it needs no action-
+# log entries; the spawned terminals ride the topology section of the T1
+# hash). Every spawn is E31-valid: connectable-within-span of a junction +
+# min-separated from every node/pipe, invalid candidates rejection-sampled
+# from the same rng stream (bounded, deterministic). Routers are NEVER
+# director-spawned (3.5 amendment) — the player places them (the `place`
+# directive below), and growth proceeds outward from the mesh.
+#
+# Era 1 (email-era, no streaming surge — the demand director spawns nothing
+# with a single residential sink, so this golden pins GROWTH ALONE: no packet
+# noise, no crisis). The player extends the mesh mid-run (place a router at
+# 1000 ms — a LOGGED Cmd_Place_Router, apply tick 21) + draws the fixture
+# router to the placed one (the new houses are connectable — the story's
+# launchable increment).
+#
+# T1 pins (replay gate + manifest): every per-tick hash, including the growth
+# windows (ticks 120, 240, ...) where the topology gains a node. T2 captures:
+# 5500 ms (t110 — the STATIC start, one window before the first spawn),
+# 15000 ms (t300 — the first two spawns), 45000 ms (t900 — mid-growth), and
+# 88000 ms (t1760 — the settled grown map, after the last spawn at t1680).
+seed 42
+era 1
+run 90000ms
+growth on
+at 1000ms place router_basic 34 15
+at 2000ms draw 1 3 standard
+at 2500ms draw 0 1 standard
+capture at 5500ms
+capture at 15000ms
+capture at 45000ms
+capture at 88000ms
+expect hash stable
